+// [Dauntless Reforged Revival, 0016] An always-relevant weapon must not be distance-culled.
+//
+// 0015's [WeaponRoute] line (17 Oct, 03:43) shows that the hammer is not dormant: it is registered with
+// flags58=0x88, bAlwaysRelevant set, so the route puts it in the graph's global AlwaysRelevantNode, at
+// loc=(0,0,0), the point it is spawned at. The armour and lantern (flags58=0x80) take the spatial route.
+// The global node still applies the class cull distance (225000000 = 15000 units squared), and it measures
+// it from FGlobalActorReplicationInfo::WorldLocation (+0x08), which only the spatial grid keeps up to
+// date. For an actor in the global node it stays at the spawn point, the world origin, so the hammer is
+// culled for any player more than 15000 units from the origin: the hunt map's start (-18111,16119) is
+// 24000 away, the city's start is close enough. This is the same defect the PlayerRole and PlayerState
+// routes above already correct by clearing the cull distance. A weapon on the global route now gets the
+// same correction at registration, and the tick-time check in MpWakeUnsentPawnWeapons also clears it,
+// globally and in each connection's snapshot, for a player's current weapon that was never sent.
+// DISABLE_WEAPON_CULL_FIX.flag turns both off.
+static bool MpWeaponCullFixEnabled() {
+    static int s_enabled = -1;
+    if (s_enabled < 0) s_enabled = MpExeRelativeFlagPresent(L"DISABLE_WEAPON_CULL_FIX.flag") ? 0 : 1;
+    return s_enabled == 1;
+}
